    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d326-a1-a33">

                <pb facs="0521" n="481" sameAs="frus:frus1865p1/pg481"/>

                <head>[Enclosure No. 33.]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Private Secretary’s
                            Office,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-01-13"><hi rendition="#italic">
                                February</hi> 13, 1865</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> In acknowledging the receipt of your letter
                    of this date, I am directed by his excellency to acquaint you that the matter to
                    which it more particularly refers, and which was first brought under his notice
                    in your letter of the 10th instant, has engaged, and continues to engage, the
                    earnest attention of the colonial government.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>H. L. WARDE,<hi rendition="#italic">Private
                    Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">William Blanchard,</hi> Esq.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
